segments.script:
Watch me read this the way a careful reader does. The passage opens: “Now does he feel
His secret murders sticking on his hands;
Now minutely revolts upbraid his faith-breach;
Those he commands move only in command,
Nothing in love: now does he feel his title
Hang loose about him, like a g” I stop and ask: what is the author doing here, and how does it connect to the tyrant's weakening grip? I circle “revolts”, one of today's words, and ask why the author chose it over a plainer word. When I find imagery, I underline it and write its effect in the margin, then I check my idea against the next sentence.
